<p>AI model files are downloaded from
    <a href="https://huggingface.co/">Hugging Face</a>, and the list of available models is fetched from GitHub. These
        are one-way downloads of static files — we do not log your identity, IP address, or device identifiers in
        connection with them. Hugging Face and GitHub receive the technical information inherent to any download (such as
        your IP address) and handle it under their own privacy policies (see section 5).</p>
<p>The app asks for microphone access only so you can dictate messages or talk to the Voice Assistant. Audio is
    recorded only while you are speaking to the app, is transcribed on your device, and is never sent anywhere.</p>
<h2>3. Crash &amp; performance diagnostics</h2>
<p>NobodyWho Chat uses
    <a href="https://sentry.io/">Sentry</a>, a third-party diagnostics service. If the app crashes or encounters an error,
        Sentry receives a technical report so we can find and fix bugs. For a small random sample of sessions, Sentry also
        receives performance measurements (such as how long a screen takes to load) so we can find and fix slowdowns.</p>
<p>These reports contain only non-personal technical information such as the type of error, the line of code where
    it occurred, the screen being shown, timing measurements, the name of the AI model in use, the app version, the
    operating system version, and the device model. They do
    <strong>not</strong>
    contain your prompts, your messages, AI responses, your conversation history, your voice, your web searches, your
    name, your email, or any other information that could identify you personally.</p>
<p>Diagnostic data is processed by Sentry on our behalf and is used solely to diagnose and fix stability and
    performance problems. Sentry's handling of this data is governed by
    <a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/">Sentry's Privacy Policy</a>. We do not use
            diagnostic data for advertising, profiling, or any purpose other than improving the app.</p>
<h2>4. How the app works</h2>
<p>NobodyWho Chat runs a language model entirely on your device's processor. When you type or dictate a message, your
    input is processed on your device's chip, a response is generated on your device's chip, and the result is displayed on
    your device's screen.</p>
<p>There are no API calls to external AI services, no relay servers, and no logging of your prompts or responses. Your
    conversation is never sent over a network. Your messages are never used for diagnostics.</p>
<p>Once an AI model is downloaded, the app functions with no internet connection. You can use it on a plane in airplane
    mode, in a remote wilderness, or anywhere without cellular or Wi-Fi coverage. (Diagnostic reports, when they occur, are
    sent the next time your device has a network connection.)</p>
<h3>Web search (optional)</h3>
<p>Web search is off by default. When you turn it on, the AI model on your device writes one or a few short search
    queries based on your message and the last few turns of the conversation. Only those queries are sent to a
    third-party search engine (DuckDuckGo, Brave Search, or Mojeek), together with a region setting so results match
    your language. Your full conversation is never sent.</p>
<p>The search engine is queried through a private, in-app browser. The app then downloads the text of the top
    results directly from those websites to read them, and loads the small website icons shown next to sources from
    DuckDuckGo's icon service. The search engines and websites involved receive your queries or page requests along with
    standard technical information such as your IP address, and handle them under their own privacy policies. We do not
    operate any server in this process and never receive your searches.</p>
<p>The in-app browser runs in private mode: cookies and site data set during a search are discarded afterwards. If a
    search engine asks you to complete a verification check (CAPTCHA), it is shown in that browser and handled by the
    search engine's verification provider (such as Cloudflare, hCaptcha, or Google reCAPTCHA); that interaction is between
    you and those services. Search results and sources are stored on your device with the conversation and are deleted
    when you delete it.</p>
<h3>Online tools</h3>
<p>Some AI models can use built-in tools to answer certain questions. Most tools (such as unit conversions) run
    entirely on your device. A few look up live information: weather uses
    <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo</a>, encyclopedia lookups use
    <a href="https://www.wikipedia.org/">Wikipedia</a>, stock quotes use Yahoo Finance, and currency rates use
    <a href="https://frankfurter.dev/">Frankfurter</a>. When one of these is used, only the specific item being looked up
        (for example a city name or a stock symbol) is sent to that service — never your conversation.</p>
<h2>5. Data sharing &amp; third parties</h2>
<p>We share no personal data with any third party, because we collect none. There are no advertising SDKs, no analytics
    platforms, and no data brokers involved in the operation of this app.</p>
